// "Manège Mousseline": a fair on its hill, a sunny afternoon, its big coasters above the lawns
// (issue #112, the 14th circuit, the second of the fourth cup), after the guide « Conception des
// circuits » (docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1650 m a lap, turning left, from
// 10 to 30 m up: the start straight on the fair's main alley, 10 m up; the carousel's S, two
// hairpins (right, left); a tight corner to the left; the climb west up the coaster's hill (27 %,
// in anti-gravity); the risky jump's corner on the top, 30 m up (a tight corner to the left, its
// inside a drop, that a ramp crosses), its wide landing, south; then the lacets down through the
// fair, three hairpins (right, left, right): the terrace of the stalls and its drop of 4 m, the
// alley of the games; the low lawn; the last hairpin, the bulge round a giant tree, whose hidden
// road runs straight behind a curtain of tall grass; the last corner, that the grass bridge
// crosses behind a panel that breaks under a boost; a bump on the way back to the line. Six
// hairpins of 165 to 180° (a Normal bot drifts them), the bulge's S (right 75°, left 150°, right
// 75°), four tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve, one long straight. The pieces of the
// shortcuts (the jump's corner and its landing; the last hairpin, the bulge, the last corner and
// their paths, the way back to the line) are the Bourg Bouillotte's, mirrored (the Coteau
// Citrouille's, the Corniche Cannelle's: their gains and their hiding were tuned), with other
// covers; the rest is new.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs (hairpins of 20 and 22 m, tight corners of 18 m), its
// points every 8 m along it (the parameters below follow them). The generator is not in the
// repository: the Bourg's pieces are copied, moved and mirrored.
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north,
// -Z), then turn right. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Manège Mousseline",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the fair on its hill (`assets/data/biomes.ron`, Kenney's Coaster Kit
    // and giant treats of the Food Kit), the same every time (seed), and pieces placed by hand:
    // checkered flags at the start line; stalls along the main alley; a giant looping of the
    // big coaster by the jump's corner; a giant tree in the bulge.
    biome: "Foire",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "amusement-park-stage",
    decor_seed: 112,
    // Issue #195: the fair's hill (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), and it hugs the road (`embank`, rise
    // over run: about 31°, as on the circuits of issue #211): the road, 10 to 30 m above the
    // valley, is carried by the hill up to its walls, instead of skirts down to the valley. The
    // voids stay (the jump's corner, the bulge, the last corner: 6 m under the road at least).
    terrain: (height: 31.0, scale: 140.0, floor: 0.25, rock: (0.62, 0.52, 0.46), embank: 0.6),
    props: [
        (model: "racing-kit/flagCheckers", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        // The stalls of the main alley, on the start straight.
        (model: "coaster-kit/stall-food", at: 2.5, side: Right, height: 3.6, radius: 2.2, gap: 0.5),
        (model: "coaster-kit/stall-drinks", at: 6.0, side: Right, height: 3.8, radius: 2.2, gap: 0.5),
        (model: "coaster-kit/stall-information", at: 2.0, side: Left, height: 3.4, radius: 2.2, gap: 0.5),
        (model: "coaster-kit/stall-food", at: 5.5, side: Left, height: 3.6, radius: 2.2, gap: 0.5),
        // A giant looping of the big coaster by the jump's corner, over the lawns.
        (model: "coaster-kit/coaster-steel-looping", at: 57.204, side: Right, height: 16.0, radius: 8.0, gap: 2.0),
        // A giant tree in the bulge.
        (model: "coaster-kit/tree-large", at: 172.216, side: Left, height: 22.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
